</nav></div></header><main><section class="zk-hero"><div class="zk-wrap"><div class="zk-eyebrow">CUSTOMER STORIES</div><h1>Real Decisions. Practical Lessons.</h1><p>A growing library of approved customer and partner stories showing how enterprise workforce-data-collection challenges are approached in practice.</p></div></section><section class="zk-section"><div class="zk-wrap"><div class="zk-section-head"><div class="zk-eyebrow">CUSTOMER PROOF</div><h2>Customer Stories, Done the Right Way.</h2><p>Approved stories will show how customers and partners solve real workforce-data-collection challenges with ZKTeco WFM.</p></div><div class="zk-grid-2"><article class="zk-card zk-case-placeholder"><div class="zk-tag">CASE STUDY COMING SOON</div><h3>Workday Enterprise Deployments</h3><p>How organizations approach time-clock modernization, time &amp; labor collection, implementation and long-term operations in Workday environments.</p></article><article class="zk-card zk-case-placeholder"><div class="zk-tag">CASE STUDY COMING SOON</div><h3>Software Partner Expansion</h3><p>How workforce software companies extend their platforms with enterprise time-clock technology, Android, APIs and cloud connectivity.</p></article><article class="zk-card zk-case-placeholder"><div class="zk-tag">CASE STUDY COMING SOON</div><h3>Complex Frontline Workforces</h3><p>How organizations with demanding environments evaluate authentication, connectivity, labor data, durability and employee workflows.</p></article><article class="zk-card zk-case-placeholder"><div class="zk-tag">CASE STUDY COMING SOON</div><h3>Legacy Modernization</h3><p>How enterprises evaluate a move from aging time-clock estates to a more flexible and maintainable workforce edge.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="zk-section alt"><div class="zk-wrap"><div class="zk-section-head"><div class="zk-eyebrow">WHAT WE WILL FOCUS ON</div><h2>Evidence, Not Marketing Theater.</h2><p>Each story will focus on the challenge, decision, implementation and lessons learned—with customer approval.</p></div><div class="zk-grid-3"><article class="zk-card"><h3>The Challenge</h3><p>What the customer needed to solve and why the existing approach was not enough.</p></article><article class="zk-card"><h3>The Decision</h3><p>The architectural, operational and workforce considerations that shaped the approach.</p></article><article class="zk-card"><h3>The Outcome</h3><p>Approved results, lessons learned and what other organizations can take away.</p></article></div></div></section>
